{
  "guid": "logi",
  "name": "Logic",
  "short_description": "Performs various logical operations",
  "description": "This algorithm is based on the disting mk4 algorithm of the same name. Each channel of the algorithm is independent and performs logical operations on its X & Y inputs. The following operations are available: AND, OR, XOR, NAND, NOR, XNOR, SR flip-flop, D flip-flop, greater than, less than. The SR flip-flop is set high by a rising edge on input X, and cleared low by a rising edge on input Y. The D flip-flop takes the level of input X on a rising edge on input Y. The global parameters set the threshold and hysteresis of the input comparators which generate logical signals from arbitrary CVs. Complex logical operations can be constructed by combining operations. The inputs of each channel can be set to the outputs of other channels, allowing you to chain them internally to the algorithm.",
  "categories": [
    "Logic",
    "Comparator",
    "Digital"
  ],
